ChildVault_executeRebalance
  ├── when the contract is paused
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when caller does not have REBALANCE_OPERATOR_ROLE
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when recovery exists
  │   └── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
  ├── when rebalance nonce is not greater than the last handled nonce
  │   └── it should revert with ChildVault__InvalidRebalanceNonce
  ├── when withdraw from the active adapter fails
  │   ├── when adapter reverts
  │   │   ├── it should emit failure without bridging
  │   │   ├── it should store rebalance withdraw recovery
  │   │   ├── it should emit RebalanceWithdrawRecoveryStored
  │   │   └── when rebalance withdraw recovery already exists
  │   │       ├── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
  │   │       └── when recovery state already exists
  │   │           └── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
  │   └── when adapter returns zero
  │       └── it should revert with BaseVault__NoZeroAmount
  ├── when rebalance is to the same child
  │   ├── when the target protocol adapter is not registered
  │   │   └── it should revert with BaseVault__NoAdapterRegistered
  │   ├── it should emit ActiveProtocolAdapterSet
  │   ├── it should update the last handled rebalance nonce
  │   ├── when target deposit adapter reverts
  │   │   ├── it should emit RebalanceDepositFailure
  │   │   ├── it should store rebalance deposit recovery
  │   │   └── when recovery state already exists
  │   │       └── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
  └── when rebalance is to a remote child
      ├── it should withdraw from the active adapter
      ├── it should bridge to the target child
      ├── it should emit ActiveProtocolAdapterCleared
      └── when ccipSend reverts
          ├── when the amount exceeds the token-pool capacity
          │   └── it should revert atomically without storing recovery
          └── otherwise
              └── it should store CCIP send recovery
